**Beta.** svolder has been tested against a fake device and a Bluetooth simulator that speaks the
Forkbeard protocol, and has not yet driven real Schiit hardware. Before you plug in, turn the
volume down and start low. Try it with cheap headphones or speakers first, and keep headphones off
your ears while you try a new device or a new version. Cap the volume for the web UI, MQTT and MCP
with `max_volume_db`. If something goes wrong, run `svolder daemon stop` and tell us in an
[issue](https://github.com/RRAlex/svolder/issues), with the output of `svolder doctor`. The
[README](https://github.com/RRAlex/svolder#before-you-plug-in) has the details.

@CHANGELOG@

**Install**

- Debian, Ubuntu, Raspberry Pi OS (64-bit): `sudo apt install ./svolder_@VERSION@_amd64.deb`, or
  `sudo apt install ./svolder_@VERSION@_arm64.deb` on a Raspberry Pi or another arm64 machine.
- Fedora, RHEL: `sudo dnf install ./svolder-@VERSION@-1.x86_64.rpm`
- Arch: download `PKGBUILD` and your architecture's tarball into an empty folder and run
  `makepkg -si`; `yay -S svolder-bin` once the package is on the AUR.
- Nix: `nix run github:RRAlex/svolder/v@VERSION@` or
  `nix profile install github:RRAlex/svolder/v@VERSION@`
- Any Linux: unpack `svolder-@VERSION@-x86_64-linux.tar.gz` or
  `svolder-@VERSION@-aarch64-linux.tar.gz`; the binaries are static and need only BlueZ.

A package enables nothing; each user turns the daemon on with
`systemctl --user enable --now svolderd.socket svolderd.service` (from a tarball: put the binaries
on `PATH` and run `svolder daemon install`). On a machine nobody logs in to, such as a Raspberry Pi
beside the DAC, `loginctl enable-linger $USER` keeps the user's units running after a reboot.

**Files**

| File | For |
| --- | --- |
| `svolder_@VERSION@_amd64.deb` | Debian, Ubuntu and relatives on x86_64 |
| `svolder_@VERSION@_arm64.deb` | Raspberry Pi OS (64-bit), Debian and Ubuntu on arm64 |
| `svolder-@VERSION@-1.x86_64.rpm` | Fedora, RHEL and relatives on x86_64 |
| `svolder-@VERSION@-x86_64-linux.tar.gz` | any x86_64 Linux: static binaries, docs, unit templates |
| `svolder-@VERSION@-aarch64-linux.tar.gz` | any arm64 Linux: the same for arm64 |
| `svolder-@VERSION@-source.tar.gz` | our source plus every dependency's, for offline and reproducible builds |
| `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES` | the licence of everything inside the binaries |
| `PKGBUILD` | Arch's `makepkg`, around the two tarballs |
| `SHA256SUMS` | the checksum of every other file here |

**Check the download:** `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`. To rebuild it, `make repro-check` in a clone of the
tag (`git clone --branch v@VERSION@ https://github.com/RRAlex/svolder`) builds every file twice and
checks the two builds agree; then `cmp target/dist/SHA256SUMS` with the release's `SHA256SUMS`. On an
x86_64 machine the arm64 half needs QEMU user-mode emulation
(`sudo apt install qemu-user qemu-user-binfmt`).
